# Project Rules & Guidelines

## 1. Code Organization & File Management

### File Length
- **Max 500 lines per file**.
- If longer → refactor into smaller, logically grouped files.
- **Visual cue**: Use a chart or diagram to show module dependencies when splitting large files.

### Folder Structure
- Organize by **feature / screen / module**.
- Subfolders for components, views, services, utils.
- **Visual cue**: Tree diagram of folder structure improves clarity for new developers.

### Localization
- Each screen/feature → **own localization file** (English & Arabic).
- **Avoid one giant file** for the whole app.
- Key naming consistent by screen/feature.
- **Chart suggestion**: table mapping screens → keys → translations for quick reference.

### Documentation
- Include small visual diagrams:
    - Component hierarchy flowchart.
    - Data flow diagram for complex screens.
- Notes on design patterns & caveats.

### Compiler-Friendly Views
- Keep views modular & lightweight.
- Break complex screens into reusable subviews.
- **Chart suggestion**: component tree to illustrate subview structure.

## 2. Design & UX Principles

### Aesthetic
- **Minimalist, modern, slightly playful**.
- **Whitespace first**: let content breathe.
- Avoid gradients, heavy textures, noisy backgrounds.

### Layout
- Flexible, grid-aligned layouts.
- Consistent spacing, padding, alignment.
- Cards & containers to group related elements.
- **Chart suggestion**: grid alignment diagram for consistent spacing.

### Typography
- Clean sans-serif fonts.
- Hierarchy: headings → bold/larger, body → regular.
- Left-aligned unless design demands otherwise.

### Color Palette
- Neutral backgrounds, subtle section separation.
- Primary accent: buttons, links, highlights.
- Ensure contrast ratio > 4.5:1 for accessibility.
- **Chart suggestion**: color swatch table showing usage per element.

### UI Components
- **Buttons**: filled (primary), outlined/subtle (secondary).
- **Inputs**: rounded, padded, clear borders.
- **Cards**: light background, subtle shadow, rounded corners.
- **Icons**: thin line, consistent sizing, accent or monochrome.
- **Content blocks**: limited width, context-aligned.

### Visual Style
- No heavy shadows/gradients.
- Subtle animations only.
- Ample whitespace for calm, readable screens.

## 3. Modern Interaction Patterns

### Interactive
- Beyond static lists/pickers.
- Immediate feedback for taps & selections.

### Visual Hierarchy
- Use spacing, typography, and cards to guide focus.
- **Chart suggestion**: attention flow diagram showing which areas user notices first.

### Context-Aware
- Only show relevant options to reduce clutter.

### Tactile & Responsive
- Haptic feedback for taps & primary actions.
- Example:
    - Light tap → selection.
    - Success → form submission.

## 4. Key UI Implementations

### Card-Based Selection
- Replace pickers with tappable cards.
- Include icon, title, description.
- Selected card → accent border & tinted icon.
- **Chart idea**: comparison table of old picker vs card design.

### Date & Repetition Controls
- **Weekly picker**: horizontal tappable day buttons, accent-filled selected day.
- **Monthly picker**: dropdown to save space.
- **Chart idea**: timeline or calendar visualization for clarity.

### Conditional Sections
- Optional content wrapped in rounded, subtle cards.
- Smooth transitions on appear/disappear.

### Haptic Feedback
- Light taps on cards/day pickers.
- Success vibration for primary actions.

## 5. Localization Guidelines
- One file per screen/feature.
- Consistent key naming per screen.
- Easy editing & translation.
- **Chart idea**: matrix chart showing screens → keys → translation completeness.

## 6. Development Best Practices
- Small, modular views.
- Split complex logic into smaller functions/components.
- Consider tactile haptics.
- **Readability & maintainability > clever complexity**.
- **Chart idea**: modular dependency diagram to visualize code coupling.

## 7. Style Summary Checklist
- [ ] Minimalist, clean, modern
- [ ] Organized folder & file structure
- [ ] Screen-based localization
- [ ] Card-based content grouping
- [ ] Interactive, context-aware controls
- [ ] Subtle haptics
- [ ] Modular, compiler-friendly views
- [ ] Documentation + diagrams
- [ ] Charts for clarity when needed

## 8. Recommended Charts & Visual Aids

| Use Case | Chart/Visual Type | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Folder structure | Tree diagram | Quick navigation & clarity |
| Localization | Table mapping screens → keys → translations | Translation overview |
| Component hierarchy | Flowchart | Easy onboarding & maintenance |
| Attention flow | Heatmap-like diagram | Design validation |
| Pickers vs Cards | Comparison table | UX decision rationale |
| Modular dependencies | Dependency diagram | Avoid coupling & complexity |

## Overall Design Style
Make the design in the style of: **clean, flat, white spaces, elegant, playful and highly organized with no clutter, easy to read, easy to understand**.

## 9. Platform-Adaptive UI Guidelines

> [!CAUTION]
> **CRITICAL: Platform-Adaptive Design Required**
>
> All UI components MUST be platform-adaptive:
> - **iOS**: Use Cupertino widgets (`cupertino_native`)
> - **Android**: Use Material widgets
>
> This ensures native look and feel on each platform.

### iOS Implementation (cupertino_native)

Use `cupertino_native` for iOS specific UI elements.

### Tab Bar
Overlay this at the bottom of your page.

```dart
int _tabIndex = 0;

// Overlay this at the bottom of your page
CNTabBar(
  items: const [
    CNTabBarItem(label: 'Home', icon: CNSymbol('house.fill')),
    CNTabBarItem(label: 'Profile', icon: CNSymbol('person.crop.circle')),
    CNTabBarItem(label: 'Settings', icon: CNSymbol('gearshape.fill')),
  ],
  currentIndex: _tabIndex,
  onTap: (i) => setState(() => _tabIndex = i),
)
```

### Popup Menu
```dart
final items = [
  const CNPopupMenuItem(label: 'New File', icon: CNSymbol('doc', size: 18)),
  const CNPopupMenuItem(label: 'New Folder', icon: CNSymbol('folder', size: 18)),
  const CNPopupMenuDivider(),
  const CNPopupMenuItem(label: 'Rename', icon: CNSymbol('rectangle.and.pencil.and.ellipsis', size: 18)),
];

CNPopupMenuButton(
  buttonLabel: 'Actions',
  items: items,
  onSelected: (index) {
    // Handle selection
  },
)
```

### Icons
```dart
// Monochrome symbol
const CNIcon(symbol: CNSymbol('star'));

// Multicolor / hierarchical options are also supported
const CNIcon(
  symbol: CNSymbol('paintpalette.fill'),
  mode: CNSymbolRenderingMode.multicolor,
)
```

### Buttons
```dart
CNButton(
  label: 'Press me',
  onPressed: () {},
)

// Icon button variant
CNButton.icon(
  icon: const CNSymbol('heart.fill'),
  onPressed: () {},
)
```

### Segmented Control
```dart
int _index = 0;

CNSegmentedControl(
  labels: const ['One', 'Two', 'Three'],
  selectedIndex: _index,
  onValueChanged: (i) => setState(() => _index = i),
)
```

### Switch
```dart
bool _on = true;

CNSwitch(
  value: _on,
  onChanged: (v) => setState(() => _on = v),
)
```

### Slider
```dart
double _value = 50;

CNSlider(
  value: _value,
  min: 0,
  max: 100,
  onChanged: (v) => setState(() => _value = v),
)
```